        <font color="#000000" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica" size="2"> Just a note for those of us who are Binding-impaired, you can now get bound in the gypsy camp in NK.  Just in case. :)</P><P>I've hunted in Splitpaw quite a bit and I can tell you that the trains can be much bigger than "mini-trains".  I know, I've started a few.  Unless you have a couple groups or feel really lucky, low-30s should not go past the double doors.  The Nisch gnolls are healers and will heal themselves continuously, so you better have someone that can interrupt them or it makes for a LONG battle.  Likewise, the Rosch gnolls are enchanters and WILL charm people, so have someone ready to dispell.  If you stay before the double doors then you won't run into these guys.</P><P>There are about 3 good camp spots before the double doors.  Move slowly and clear each room before you move too far away from the exit and get the feel for the spawns.</P><P>Splitpaw is a very fun, challenging dungeon, which is why I think its usually empty.  People don't want challenge, they want easy experience.  When you fight your way to the back of Splitpaw you really feel like you have accomplished something.<BR> <BR>I don't know if I will be playing on Friday night or have already promised to do something, but I would love to be a tour guide to Paw.</P><P>Good hunting.<BR>Norbert<BR>Nomadic Revellers<BR>43 Warrior</P><P>Edited by - norbert on 10 Apr 2001  12:49:11<a href="#top"><img src="icon_go_up.gif" height=15 width=15 border="0" align="right" alt="Go to Top of Page"></a></font></td>
